# Agent knowledge base

This repo’s agent vault lives at `docs/`.

## After the IDE plan is approved

1. Read `docs/playbook.md`, then keep `docs/processes/definition-of-done.md` open until the end.
2. For product shape, skim `docs/app/purpose-and-flows.md` and `docs/app/layout.md`. Touching a tool panel → also `docs/app/tools.md` and `docs/app/invoke-surface.md`. Internals → `docs/app/systems/overview.md`.
3. Commands / env / release → `docs/app/run-test-lint.md`, `docs/app/config-env.md`, `docs/app/publish.md`.
4. Verify runtime work per `docs/app/verify.md` (not code-reading alone).
5. Before the human opens a PR → `docs/processes/pre-review-qa.md`.
6. After meaningful feature work (or when the human asks) → load skill `compounding-knowledge` (source: `docs/skills/compounding-knowledge/SKILL.md`). Do not treat every agent stop as a vault-update trigger.

Load other vault skills from `docs/skills/*/SKILL.md` when the task matches (also mirrored under `.cursor/skills/` for discovery). Follow Obsidian `[[wikilinks]]` only when you need that file.

## Hard limits

- Do not open, merge, or approve pull requests.
- Do not invent passing tests that skip the real path.
- Do not put secrets in files or chat.
- Stop all servers, background processes, and application runs started by the agent before being done.
- Prefer editing an existing vault note over creating a duplicate.
- ADRs under `docs/adrs/` are optional background — do not block on them unless the human asks.
- Do not say done while Definition of Done still has unchecked items you can satisfy.
